= Blockchain — Simple =

A blockchain is a shared ledger copied across a network. Records are grouped into blocks, and each block is cryptographically linked to earlier blocks. Network rules decide which updates are accepted.

'''Important boundary:''' blockchain ≠ cryptocurrency.

